  "decision": "Retain sequential parallelism1; shared application-independent compiler graph is supported by all three paired cold reductions and actual invalidation/security/image gates. Final integrated required CI remains necessary before merge.",
  "limits": [
    "Results apply to the frozen application/source and Dockerfile experiment, not byte-identical final integration artifacts; later application tests, main features, migration renumbering and caller fixes change build contexts. Final images require their own normal smoke/scans.",
    "Each pair shares host/hardware/image/effective limits; CPU models and host image/memory vary across pairs and are retained. Three pairs are not a production latency SLO or broad hardware distribution.",
    "Warm results use one disposable runner-local builder; no cross-job/external cache is imported/exported. No private signing key/cache is uploaded.",
    "Resource samples are host observations, not isolated container CPU/RSS measurements. First-variant loaded images remain during second variant, so disk occupancy is order-dependent.",
    "Runner seconds and fixed resource budgets are cost proxies, not billed monetary charges; full experiment includes setup, full gates and one-time real invalidation compilation. No whole-CI percentage reduction is claimed."
  ],
